> [!abstract] The connective tissue of the Operating System.
> [[The Operating System]] explains *why* the OS exists and [[Schema — Data Model]] defines *how the data is shaped*. This note is the **skeleton**: it ties every existing piece to the four things you actually want to know, names exactly what's missing to compute each, gives the formula layer to compute them, and sets the build order. Read this when you're deciding *what to work on next*.

## 0. The one-line model

Orderliness is a **bill you pay daily** ([[The Real Problem Manifesto|Manifesto]]). The OS exists to make that bill honest, so the **surplus** above it — the thing that buys [[Part 2.0 - Self, Reality and Order|Design]] — can be measured. Everything below serves one equation:

$$\text{Monthly Nut} \;=\; \text{Living (E)} \;+\; \text{Protocol \& Foundational (F)} \;+\; \text{Executional} \quad\longrightarrow\quad \text{Surplus} = \text{Income} - \text{Nut}$$

Once the Nut is real, the freedom numbers (Buckets 1 & 3) and the on-par income target fall straight out of it.

