## 3. The calc layer (formula spec)

This is the missing computation layer, written so it maps 1:1 onto Obsidian Base formulas now and the parked Postgres views later.

### 3.1 Per-product cost & forecast (fix + extend)
```
effective_daily   = daily_dose × days_per_week / 7          # mg (or unit) burned per day
total_units_mg    = package_size × base_dose                # if package_size is servings; else convert
cost_per_mg       = cost_per_bottle / total_units_mg         # FIX: replaces cost_per_bottle/package_size
cost_per_day      = effective_daily × cost_per_mg
cost_per_month    = cost_per_day × 30.44
days_until_empty  = stock_on_hand_in_mg / effective_daily    # requires stock unit normalised first
landed_cost       = cost_per_bottle + allocated_shipping + fees   # from Source note
```
Guard: only sum notes where `count_in_total = true` and `status = active`. Peptides excluded (INDEXA).

### 3.2 Roll-ups (the ledger)
```
Protocol_burn_monthly = Σ cost_per_month  over active, counted products      # goal 1 (F, protocol part)
Living_monthly        = Σ eff_monthly     over Overheads where category=Living # E
Foundational_other    = gym + diagnostics + grooming + food premium           # F (non-pill)
Executional_monthly   = software/subscriptions + courses + device sinking fund # X
Monthly_Nut           = Living + (Protocol_burn + Foundational_other) + Executional

# goal 2
Stockup_this_year = Σ (qty_to_buy × landed_cost_per_unit) over restock ∈ {Buy now, Buy this month}
Recurring_burn    = Protocol_burn_monthly        # what continues after stock is built
```
> [!note] E vs F vs X tagging
> Overheads already have `category`. Add a one-word **layer** tag (E / F / X) to every Overhead and product stack so the roll-up sorts itself. Living→E; gym/diagnostics/supplements/PEDs/food→F; software/courses/devices→X.

### 3.3 Freedom math (goal 4) — targets locked
```
EF_monthly        = Living(E) + Foundational(F)        # exclude Executional & Lifestyle from the floor
Emergency_6mo     = EF_monthly × 6                     # the "6-month optionality" target (Bucket 1)
Freedom_24mo      = EF_monthly × 24 × 1.06             # ~3%/yr × 2yr inflation hedge (Bucket 3)
Surplus_monthly   = Income - Monthly_Nut
Months_to_Freedom = Freedom_24mo / Surplus_monthly     # the headline "how long" number
On_par check      = compare EPF balance to Coast-FI / RIA tier  # Part 3.0
```
Sanity-check `EF_monthly` against *Belanjawanku* (~RM1,970–2,800/mo single working adult, Klang Valley); if far below, the audit is missing items.

> [!important] The shadow-rent decision
> Living currently books **Rent RM0** (family home) and **Car RM0** (paid off). That makes today's Nut honest but the *freedom* number optimistic — if independence means market rent (~RM1,800) and a car (~RM500), the Freedom Fund roughly doubles. Recommend computing **two columns: "current floor" and "independent floor"** so the freedom target isn't fiction. (Flagged in [[QC & Gap Analysis]] Part 3.)

